# Line endings are a correctness setting, not a style preference. The design
# system's gate kit reads the lockfile as a graph and parses JSON and source as
# text; a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf` on turns every one of them into
# CRLF, and a parser that anchors on a newline then reads a line with a character
# on the end of it. `text=auto` lets git normalise the text files, and the
# lockfile is left alone because it is generated and read as a graph.

* text=auto

*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf

pnpm-lock.yaml -text
